# Gate step 1198-7q95 — data, not code.
#
# Binds the fixture for the claim-expiry sweep's channel: age and attribute a
# claim from the STATUS WRITE that set in_progress, not from the newest event
# on the row. 1065-4t7t corrected the sibling live_claims() for exactly this
# and left expire_claim_candidates() on the event channel, so one instrument
# disagreed with itself about who holds a claim — and the coordinator acted on
# the wrong half, asking a host to release work it had never held.
#
# Arms 1 and 2 are the behavioural discriminators and fail on the pre-fix
# code; arm 3 pins that the event fallback for a base-born in_progress is
# DELIBERATE and survives the fix.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the claim-expiry sweep ages and attributes from the status write, not the newest event (1198-7q95)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-expire-claims-reads-the-status-write.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the claim-expiry sweep is reading the event channel again — it would return live claims to ready and name the wrong host (1198-7q95)"
STEP_OK="claim-expiry sweep reads the status write"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:expire-claims-reads-the-status-write"
